                <pb facs="0346" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/5009: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-28T19:00:00+03:00">August 28, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 28—6:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>536. I have been officially informed that a band of some 1500 Ethiopians attacked
                    the local aerodrome night before last but were defeated. Ethiopian casualties
                    were about 200 while the Italian native troops lost 15 killed and about 40
                    wounded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
